READING — this measures TAP observability only (fs_*/ss_*):
  The host emits every composite before its input scale appears
  on a tap, because the host precomputes scales from the golden.
  A composite unit fed ONLY by the taps must therefore emit late,
  which would reorder the stream.

  BUT the taps are not the only on-tile source. The KVQ stores a
  per-record fp16 scale at store time (rtl/kvq/kvq_engine.sv:290,
  and scale_bank_store :431 for grouped keys). At CQ-8 that stored
  scale is BIT-IDENTICAL to the feeder's read-time s_k[t]/s_v[t]
  (verified over the suite tensors + 13k random tokens), so a
  store-time scale cache lets the walker emit in the host's EXACT
  order — no reorder allowance needed.

  Grouped tiers (CQ-4/CQ-4+) recompute a different read-time scale
  from the dequantized record; it is determined at store time but
  is NOT the stored per-record scale, so capturing it needs a
  feeder-equivalent commit-time amax pass. See B1_WALKER.md §4.
